  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0 (cut from upstream/main 7a5816cf).\n\nWhat changed: the stock-carry refusal in `carry_turn` named \"a lathe or mill-turn machine\" for any non-mill setup (a sinker EDM too). `CARRY_MACHINE_REFUSAL` is now the stable prefix and the new `carry_machine_refusal(kind)` appends the actual kind (\"lathe\", \"mill-turn\", \"wire EDM\", \"sinker EDM\", \"plasma\"). The refusal is exactly as strict as before.\n\nTests: `a_carry_onto_a_sinker_edm_names_the_sinker_edm_and_a_mill_still_carries`, `a_carry_on_a_lathe_or_mill_turn_is_refused_by_name_on_every_path` (now asserts the kind). Quick gate green (app suites 137 s) and clippy -D warnings on camcraft-app clean. Not exercised: wire EDM/plasma text (same helper).\n\nChangelog: Stock-carry refusal names the setup's actual machine kind instead of \"a lathe or mill-turn machine\" (#1182)\n\nFixes #1182\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
